      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#Arrays\n",
        "The central feature of NumPy is the array object class. Arrays are similar to lists in Python, except\n",
        "that every element of an array must be of the same type, typically a numeric type like float or\n",
        "int. Arrays make operations with large amounts of numeric data very fast and are generally\n",
        "much more efficient than lists."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IVF83eszd7Gl"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "a = np.array([1, 4, 5, 8], float)\n",
        "print(type(a))\n",
        "a"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "o-sIQ0MZd9nt",
        "outputId": "a4cb3f8d-edbd-4c2f-c2b5-9b5d6fcda9a3"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "<class 'numpy.ndarray'>\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "array([1., 4., 5., 8.])"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "the function array takes two arguments: the list to be converted into the array and the\n",
        "type of each member of the list."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GaKTCm0ceU1i"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "#array slicing\n",
        "a[:2]\n",
        "print(a[1:3])\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "2hdtPihOeCQd",
        "outputId": "4a8df4b9-52b1-4d1c-d882-df1259edf680"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[4. 5.]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "#array manipulation\n",
        "a[0] = 5.\n",
        "a\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "1UMKEpYqeRE9",
        "outputId": "bee0b7df-7bb7-4aac-d2e8-e321cc80ca46"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "array([5., 4., 5., 8.])"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Arrays can be multidimensional. Unlike lists, different axes are accessed using commas inside\n",
        "bracket notation. Here is an example with a two-dimensional array (e.g., a matrix):"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Enzn4u_5enW6"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "a = np.array([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]], float)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(a[0,0])\n",
        "print(a[0,1])\n",
        "a"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "_4WVHn4Geg28",
        "outputId": "dc90cad8-ce9e-4b51-825b-7fc5a48e275b"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "1.0\n",
            "2.0\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "array([[1., 2., 3.],\n",
              "       [4., 5., 6.]])"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Array slicing works with multiple dimensions in the same way as usual, applying each slice\n",
        "specification as a filter to a specified dimension. Use of a single \":\" in a dimension indicates the\n",
        "use of everything along that dimension:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zskcHHJIe5jP"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "#print(a[1,0:2])\n",
        "print(a[1,1])\n",
        "print(a[:,2])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(a[-1:,-1:])\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "OWaK1T7Wev1_",
        "outputId": "3a4db3ca-0845-4373-8455-8771b7d189a0"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "5.0\n",
            "[3. 6.]\n",
            "[[6.]]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The shape property of an array returns a tuple with the size of each array dimension:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bfKbI1NkfZYZ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "a.shape"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "VPxArj1afYov",
        "outputId": "add8c262-25f3-4cd5-bb9e-4ca882c0d7ad"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "(2, 3)"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The dtype property tells you what type of values are stored by the array:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rDqa6Plmfdsa"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "a.dtype"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "GtQsK5G1fElN",
        "outputId": "4412ca0e-2965-4851-9184-bd363fcb3656"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "dtype('float64')"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "When used with an array, the len function returns the length of the first axis:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "L4OtT77Nfnay"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "len(a)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
