    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#Other ways to create arrays\n",
        "The arange function is similar to the range function but returns an array instead of a list:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Xx1BHUCd_Wz2"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(np.arange(5, dtype=float))\n",
        "print(np.arange(1, 6, 2, dtype=int))\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dhfsceJMB0NN",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "3fedb84d-95e7-4fc9-d401-8a7b0fccdce5"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[0. 1. 2. 3. 4.]\n",
            "[1 3 5]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The functions zeros and ones create new arrays of specified dimensions filled with these\n",
        "values. These are perhaps the most commonly used functions to create new arrays:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
